---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Design system
permalink: /design-system/
summary: The tokens, type and Nunjucks components behind Dilemma for his Dragon.
---
{% from "components/page-header/page-header.njk" import pageHeader %}
{% set parchment = "#ece0c2" %}
{% set paperLight = "#f4ead2" %}

{{ pageHeader({
  kicker: "How this chronicle is made",
  title: title,
  lede: "Ink on parchment: the tokens, type and Nunjucks components behind every page of the site."
}) }}

<div class="ds wide">
  <nav class="ds-toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <p class="ds-toc__title">On this page</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#ds-how">How it works</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ds-colour">Colour</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ds-type">Typography</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ds-space">Space and width</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ds-components">Components</a>
        <ol>
          {%- for g in componentDocs %}{% for c in g.items %}
          <li><a href="#c-{{ c.slug }}">{{ c.name }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="ds-body">

    <section aria-labelledby="ds-how">
      <h2 id="ds-how">How it works</h2>
      <p>Everything is built by Eleventy in GitHub Actions and published to GitHub Pages as static files.</p>
      <dl class="ds-facts">
        <div><dt>Tokens</dt><dd><code>src/_data/tokens.js</code> holds every colour, font, size, space and width. Sass reads it as a module, <code>@use "design-tokens"</code>, and this page reads it as data, so they cannot disagree.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Custom properties</dt><dd>Each token is written out as a CSS custom property, such as <code>--color-rubric</code>. In Sass, use the helpers from <code>scss/settings</code>: <code>color(rubric)</code>, <code>space(md)</code>, <code>font(display)</code>.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Components</dt><dd>Each lives in its own folder in <code>src/_includes/components/</code>: a Nunjucks macro and, beside it, a Sass partial. Import the macro with <code>{% raw %}{% from "components/card/card.njk" import card %}{% endraw %}</code>.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Stylesheet</dt><dd><code>src/css/style.scss</code> loads the foundations, then every component partial, and compiles to one compressed file.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Adding a component</dt><dd>Create the folder with <code>name.njk</code> and <code>_name.scss</code>, add <code>@use "components/name/name"</code> to the stylesheet, and document it in <code>src/_data/componentDocs.js</code>. Its example then appears on this page.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ds-colour">
      <h2 id="ds-colour">Colour</h2>
      <p>Iron gall ink and one red, the rubric a scribe used for headings and initials, on aged paper. Contrast is measured against the page background and the raised surface.</p>
      <ul class="ds-swatches">
        {%- for c in tokens.colors %}
        <li class="ds-swatch">
          <span class="ds-swatch__chip" style="background: {{ c.value }}"></span>
          <span class="ds-swatch__name">{{ c.name }}</span>
          <code>--color-{{ c.name }}</code>
          <code>{{ c.value }}</code>
          <span class="ds-swatch__role">{{ c.role }}</span>
          {%- if not c.decorative and c.value.startsWith("#") and not c.name.startsWith("parchment") %}
          {% set onPage = c.value | contrast(parchment) %}
          {% set onLight = c.value | contrast(paperLight) %}
          <span class="ds-swatch__contrast">{{ onPage }}:1 on parchment{% if onPage >= 4.5 %} <span class="ds-pass">AA</span>{% endif %}<br>{{ onLight }}:1 on parchment-light{% if onLight >= 4.5 %} <span class="ds-pass">AA</span>{% endif %}</span>
          {%- endif %}
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ds-type">
      <h2 id="ds-type">Typography</h2>
      <p>Three typefaces, all served from the site itself.</p>
      {%- for f in tokens.fonts %}
      <div class="ds-font">
        <p class="ds-font__sample" style="font-family: var(--font-{{ f.name }})">{% if f.name == "display" %}Fog over Maiden's Vale{% elif f.name == "label" %}Entry the First · The Company{% else %}Dumpy led us to his village as the mist thickened into fog. <em>Dumpy is as Dumpy does.</em>{% endif %}</p>
        <p class="ds-font__meta"><strong>{{ f.family }}</strong> · <code>--font-{{ f.name }}</code> · {{ f.role }}</p>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}

      <h3>Scale</h3>
      <p>Body text is fluid, from 18px on phones to about 21px on wide screens. Headings scale with the viewport using <code>clamp()</code>. Fixed sizes come from the scale below.</p>
      <ul class="ds-scale">
        {%- for s in tokens.typeScale %}
        <li><span class="ds-scale__sample" style="font-size: {{ s.value }}">Bobbit stew</span><code>--size-{{ s.name }}</code> <code>{{ s.value }}</code></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ds-space">
      <h2 id="ds-space">Space and width</h2>
      <ul class="ds-space">
        {%- for s in tokens.space %}
        <li><span class="ds-space__bar" style="width: {{ s.value }}"></span><code>--space-{{ s.name }}</code> <code>{{ s.value }}</code></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <dl class="ds-facts">
        {%- for w in tokens.widths %}
        <div><dt><code>--width-{{ w.name }}</code> · {{ w.value }}</dt><dd>{{ w.role }}</dd></div>
        {%- endfor %}
        <div><dt>Breakpoints</dt><dd>{% for b in tokens.breakpoints %}<code>{{ b.name }}</code> {{ b.value }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Use <code>@include mq(lg)</code>. Layouts are fluid first and need few.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ds-components">
      <h2 id="ds-components">Components</h2>
      <p>Each example below is rendered live by the macro it documents.</p>

      {%- for g in componentDocs %}
      <h3 class="ds-group">{{ g.group }}</h3>
      {%- for c in g.items %}
      <article class="ds-component" aria-labelledby="c-{{ c.slug }}">
        <h4 id="c-{{ c.slug }}">{{ c.name }}</h4>
        <p class="ds-component__file"><code>components/{{ c.slug }}/{{ c.slug }}.njk</code> · <code>{{ c.macro }}</code></p>
        <p>{{ c.description }}</p>
        <div class="ds-example">
          {{ c.example | renderNjk | safe }}
        </div>
        <details class="ds-code">
          <summary>Nunjucks</summary>
          <pre><code>{{ c.example }}</code></pre>
        </details>
        {% if c.params.length %}
        <table class="ds-params">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">{{ c.name }} parameters</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for p in c.params %}
            <tr><td><code>{{ p.name }}</code></td><td>{{ p.type }}</td><td>{{ p.desc }}</td></tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
